CHANGE ANALYSIS (citations verified, indeterminate)
───────────────────────────────────────────────────
Cannot be established from this repository alone: depends on state only known at runtime (e.g. feature flags, request data).
The mechanisms are visible, but real observable impact depends on runtime model selection, whether callers request structured output or configure thinking budgets, the shape of Gemini responses, and whether transient errors or cancellations occur.

The Google/Gemini chat adapter expands its declared model set, changes thinking configuration sent to Gemini, improves structured-response parsing and diagnostics, and replaces its own retry loop with reliance on the Google client’s retry behavior.

Likely behavioral changes
  • Gemini requests now send a thinking budget of -1 whenever thinking configuration is enabled; because the instance default is now 0 rather than None, this configuration is included by default. Caller-supplied non-None budget values are not forwarded.
  • The adapter’s declared supported Gemini model identifiers now include Gemini 2.5 Flash, Flash Lite, and Pro.
  • Native structured-output responses can now be parsed when Gemini returns the JSON inside a complete Markdown code fence, rather than failing JSON decoding solely because of that wrapper.
  • The adapter no longer performs its own surrounding multi-attempt retry loop for a generation request; it makes the call directly and expects the Google client to provide retry behavior.

Investigate
  • Trace construction of ChatGoogle instances and determine whether callers set thinking_budget deliberately or rely on its default.
  • Inspect Google client creation and SDK configuration to establish the actual retry count, backoff policy, timeout handling, and connection lifecycle after removal of the local loop.
  • Find callers requesting structured output and map which models use native response schemas versus prompt-based JSON fallback.
  • Check how asynchronous cancellation and provider exceptions are translated for upstream callers.

Uncertain
  • No HTTP route or endpoint is shown, so it cannot be established whether any route directly or indirectly exposes these ChatGoogle changes.
  • The supplied context does not identify which application components instantiate ChatGoogle, request structured output, select the new model names, or set thinking_budget.
  • The Google SDK’s built-in retry defaults and the client configuration used by get_client() are not shown, so the effective retry count and backoff behavior cannot be established.
  • The provider meaning and model support of thinking_budget=-1 are not established by this diff, including whether it enables dynamic thinking or is rejected by any listed model.
  • The structured-output parsing change is exercised only when an output format is requested, native structured output is supported, response.parsed is absent, and response.text contains suitable JSON or a complete recognized fence.

