Code review (advisory; excluded from the verdict)
─────────────────────────────────────────────────
[P2] In ChatGoogle.ainvoke, any non-None thinking_budget supplied on the instance—including 0 or a positive integer—is discarded and the request config instead contains thinking_budget=-1.
  browser_use/llm/google/chat.py:202
  Why: ChatGoogle exposes thinking_budget as an int-or-None field. ainvoke checks only whether that field is non-None, but then assigns the constant -1 rather than the field's value, and passes the resulting config to generate_content. The diff directly changed this assignment from self.thinking_budget to -1, so the loss of explicitly supplied values is introduced…
  Impact: Caused by the change: The change replaces the previous changed-line expression {'thinking_budget': self.thinking_budget} with {'thinking_budget': -1}. Consequently, whenever self.thinking_budget is non-None, ainvoke now sends the constant -1 instead of the caller-supplied value.

